hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"22877","Arim narrated to us: Mutamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from his father: as-Sumayt narrated to us, from Abu as-Sawwar, Abu as-Sawwar narrated to him, from his uncle, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, with people following him, so I followed him with them. He said: So the people suddenly hastened. He said: And the people left me behind. He said: So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came upon me and struck me a strike, either with a palm stalk or a staff or a toothstick, and something that was with him. He said: By Allah, it did not hurt me. He said: So I spent the night, he said, or I said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, struck me only for something Allah knew in me. He said: And my soul told me to come to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in the morning. He said: So Jibril, peace be upon him, descended upon the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: Indeed you are a shepherd; do not break the horns of your flock. He said: So when we prayed dawn, or he said: we entered the morning, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: O Allah, indeed people follow me, and indeed it does not please me that they follow me. O Allah, so whoever I struck or reviled, make it for him an expiation and a reward, or he said: forgiveness and mercy, or as he said."
